        "PMC10708198::web::020::relevance_of_this_study_for_processing_a"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The precipitates generated by oxygen and nitrogen are intrinsically brittle.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Grain-boundary precipitates act as stress concentrators and crack-initiation sites under mechanical loading.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Impurity-induced precipitation changes the fracture mode from ductile to brittle.",
